  "constraints": [
    "No sensor data must be interpreted as UNKNOWN rather than zero.",
    "Generator OFF is not evidence of transfer bus dead; use Electrical V7 evaluate().bus.",
    "Conventional N2 and Fuel Flow draw DC1/DC2, EIS channels have different functional supplies.",
    "MRG indicates conventional oil pressure gauge can freeze on AC transfer loss.",
    "EIS secondary functional feeds do not prove individual unit pin wiring: unknown effects stay uncertain.",
    "AVM 115VAC Transfer Bus1 per LAN conflicts with different MRG indication voltage references.",
    "Explicit effectivity-approved limits required for redline alerts; never auto-enforce examples.",
    "Functional bus assignment and EIS LRU hardware supply are distinct; P6-2 28VDC common display supply is not pinned to a specific bus.",
    "ENG1/ENG2 non-EIS N2 and FF follow DC1/DC2 after BUS TRANSFER logic, not raw GEN1/GEN2 ON BUS detents.",
    "Engine oil indicators follow Transfer Bus1/2 physical power, so backfeed via BUS TRANSFER AUTO is effective even with one engine generator unselected.",
    "Vibration both engines use the Transfer Bus1 consumer circuit; AVM signal conditioner 115VAC vs AVM indication 28VAC is an explicit LAN/MRG voltage conflict.",
    "Primary EIS failures must not bypass the technical backend through direct, raw ECU pointer updates."
  ],
